## Verification

- `rake test` in each of `week3_capable/{boukensha,mud_manager,mud_monitor}`
  — must stay green throughout; each phase is additive (new hook/task
  classes), so existing Step-12/Phase-A–F tests should be unaffected, same
  discipline as every prior phase.
- Verify **live against the real CircleMUD**, not just fixtures, for at
  least: one full Planner→Player→Judge turn with a `:replan` verdict firing,
  one `consult_navigator` call returning a real route between two visited
  rooms, and one Chronicler digest write/read across two separate sessions
  for the same character — the project's own established bar ("verified
  live" call-outs in every prior phase doc).
- Confirm the new tasks' tool surfaces are actually restricted (Judge/
  Navigator cannot call `move`/`attack`) by attempting a denied call and
  checking `Permissions::InvalidRuleError`/dispatch rejection fires.
